{"meta": {"limit": 100, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 16}, "objects": [{"abstract": "   This document specifies a \"compact\" version of TLS 1.3 and DTLS 1.3.\n   It saves bandwidth by trimming obsolete material, tighter encoding, a\n   template-based specialization technique, and alternative\n   cryptographic techniques. cTLS is not directly interoperable with TLS\n   1.3 or DTLS 1.3 since the over-the-wire framing is different.  A\n   single server can, however, offer cTLS alongside TLS or DTLS.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ctls/", "expires": "2024-04-25T15:12:18Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 344130, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ctls", "note": "", "notify": "caw@heapingbits.net", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/344130/", "rev": "09", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/caw@heapingbits.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2023-10-23T15:12:18Z", "title": "Compact TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a \"compact\" version of TLS 1.3 and DTLS 1.3.\n   It saves bandwidth by trimming obsolete material, tighter encoding, a\n   template-based specialization technique, and alternative\n   cryptographic techniques. cTLS is not directly interoperable with TLS\n   1.3 or DTLS 1.3 since the over-the-wire framing is different.  A\n   single server can, however, offer cTLS alongside TLS or DTLS.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ctls/", "expires": "2023-09-14T22:29:41Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 341713, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ctls", "note": "", "notify": "caw@heapingbits.net", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/341713/", "rev": "08", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/caw@heapingbits.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2023-09-14T07:13:40Z", "title": "Compact TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a \"compact\" version of TLS 1.3 and DTLS 1.3.\n   It saves bandwidth by trimming obsolete material, tighter encoding, a\n   template-based specialization technique, and alternative\n   cryptographic techniques. cTLS is not directly interoperable with TLS\n   1.3 or DTLS 1.3 since the over-the-wire framing is different.  A\n   single server can, however, offer cTLS alongside TLS or DTLS.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ctls/", "expires": "2024-10-19T12:45:11Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 359923, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ctls", "note": "", "notify": "caw@heapingbits.net", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/359923/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/caw@heapingbits.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2024-04-17T12:45:11Z", "title": "Compact TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a \"compact\" version of TLS 1.3.  It is\n   isomorphic to TLS 1.3 but saves space by trimming obsolete material,\n   tighter encoding, and a template-based specialization technique. cTLS\n   is not directly interoperable with TLS 1.3, but it should eventually\n   be possible for a cTLS/TLS 1.3 server to exist and successfully\n   interoperate.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ctls/", "expires": "2020-10-28T21:10:01Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 263969, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ctls", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/263969/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2020-04-26T21:10:01Z", "title": "Compact TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a \"compact\" version of TLS 1.3.  It is\n   isomorphic to TLS 1.3 but saves space by trimming obsolete material,\n   tighter encoding, and a template-based specialization technique. cTLS\n   is not directly interoperable with TLS 1.3, but it should eventually\n   be possible for a cTLS/TLS 1.3 server to exist and successfully\n   interoperate.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ctls/", "expires": "2020-10-28T21:10:01Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 263974, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ctls", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/263974/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2020-04-27T04:03:46Z", "title": "Compact TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a \"compact\" version of TLS 1.3.  It is\n   isomorphic to TLS 1.3 but saves space by trimming obsolete material,\n   tighter encoding, and a template-based specialization technique. cTLS\n   is not directly interoperable with TLS 1.3, but it should eventually\n   be possible for a cTLS/TLS 1.3 server to exist and successfully\n   interoperate.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ctls/", "expires": "2020-10-28T21:10:01Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 274142, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ctls", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/274142/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2020-10-28T07:21:43Z", "title": "Compact TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a \"compact\" version of TLS 1.3.  It is\n   isomorphic to TLS 1.3 but saves space by trimming obsolete material,\n   tighter encoding, and a template-based specialization technique. cTLS\n   is not directly interoperable with TLS 1.3, but it should eventually\n   be possible for a cTLS/TLS 1.3 server to exist and successfully\n   interoperate.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ctls/", "expires": "2021-05-06T17:14:46Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 274626, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ctls", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 19, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/274626/", "rev": "01", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2020-11-02T18:14:46Z", "title": "Compact TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a \"compact\" version of TLS 1.3.  It is\n   isomorphic to TLS 1.3 but saves space by trimming obsolete material,\n   tighter encoding, and a template-based specialization technique. cTLS\n   is not directly interoperable with TLS 1.3, but it should eventually\n   be possible for a cTLS/TLS 1.3 server to exist and successfully\n   interoperate.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ctls/", "expires": "2021-05-06T17:14:46Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 277181, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ctls", "note": "", "notify": "caw@heapingbits.net", "pages": 19, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/277181/", "rev": "01", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/caw@heapingbits.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2020-12-02T03:16:40Z", "title": "Compact TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a \"compact\" version of TLS 1.3.  It is\n   isomorphic to TLS 1.3 but saves space by trimming obsolete material,\n   tighter encoding, and a template-based specialization technique. cTLS\n   is not directly interoperable with TLS 1.3, but it should eventually\n   be possible for a cTLS/TLS 1.3 server to exist and successfully\n   interoperate.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ctls/", "expires": "2021-11-07T01:20:24Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 286033, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ctls", "note": "", "notify": "caw@heapingbits.net", "pages": 19, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/286033/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/caw@heapingbits.net/", "states": ["/api/